                "xf": [
                  1.0,
                  0.0,
                  0.0,
                  1.0,
                  44.0,
                  1364.0
                ],
                "runs": [
                  {
                    "text": "Why URL mode: data typed in the browser (token, password, OAuth sign-in, payment) goes to the server in step 10 and never passes through the MCP client or the model. The spec requires URL mode for such data and requires the client to show the full URL and ask before opening it (step 4). Flow URLs are bearer capabilities (random UUIDv4, 1 h TTL); a production server must also bind the flow to the user who started it.",
                    "style": {
                      "font_family": "Inter",
                      "font_style": "Regular",
                      "size": 14.5,
                      "tracking": 0.0,
                      "baseline_shift": 0.0,
                      "h_scale": 100.0,
